== cli
$ cxp teams service park s001 status
   exit 0
   stdout| Waiting for the running Teams helper...
   stdout| s001: Auto park: on. Chat state: active. Idle chats can be parked automatically after the normal inactivity timeout.
$ cxp teams service park s001 status
   exit 0
   stdout| Waiting for the running Teams helper...
   stdout| s001: Auto park: off. Chat state: active. This setting survives helper restarts. When active and cooled down, this chat is read every 30 seconds, subject to read pacing and backoff. Manual park is still available.
$ cxp teams service park s001 status
   exit 0
   stdout| Waiting for the running Teams helper...
   stdout| s001: Auto park: off. Chat state: active. This setting survives helper restarts. When active and cooled down, this chat is read every 30 seconds, subject to read pacing and backoff. Manual park is still available.
$ cxp teams service park s001 off
   exit 0
   stdout| Waiting for the running Teams helper...
   stdout| s001: Auto park: off. Chat state: parked. This setting survives helper restarts. When active and cooled down, this chat is read every 30 seconds, subject to read pacing and backoff. Manual park is still available. The chat remains parked. Send `r s001` in the control chat to wake it; queued messages can then run.
$ cxp teams service park s001 on
   exit 0
   stdout| Waiting for the running Teams helper...
   stdout| s001: Auto park: on. Chat state: active. Idle chats can be parked automatically after the normal inactivity timeout.
